    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is needed",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)면 돼요** says that an action is enough, or that this is the way to proceed: 쓰다 → **쓰면 돼요** (it is enough to write), 내다 → **내면 돼요** (it is enough to pay), 가다 → **가면 돼요** (it is enough to go). The conditional ending is formed as in the previous lesson; with a stem ending in ㄹ it is kept: 살면 돼요.",
      "여기에 이름을 **쓰면 돼요** = it is enough to write your name here."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What 돼요 means",
     "texto": [
      "**돼요** is the present form of 되다 («to turn out / to be fine / to be possible»). **-(으)면 돼요** says that it is enough to meet the condition: 카드를 넣으면 돼요 = it is enough to insert the card. Distinguish **하면 돼요** (it is enough to do it) from **해도 돼요** (it is allowed to do it)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
